id: pm-vcs-phase6tmprefs
title: Retain legal tmp refs during GC and protect ref publication names
description: "Confirmed in a disposable real PM tracker: refs/metadata/retained.tmp is accepted by RefStore, omitted by listing, and skipped by reachability GC; apply deletes its still-referenced payload. GC also skips valid tmp-named directories. Atomic publication uses a process-shaped tmp name that can collide with a valid ref."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T16:56:40.572Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T23:15:47.736Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:49:34.048Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T22:03:12.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: GC and listing retain every legal tmp-named ref and directory; corrupt tmp refs refuse deletion; atomic ref temporary files occupy only the reserved lock namespace and never overwrite a valid ref; independent behavioural revert regressions fail.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
severity: high
repro_steps: "Confirmed in a disposable real PM tracker: refs/metadata/retained.tmp is accepted by RefStore, omitted by listing, and skipped by reachability GC; apply deletes its still-referenced payload. GC also skips valid tmp-named directories. Atomic publication uses a process-shaped tmp name that can collide with a valid ref."
resolution: GC/listing retain legal tmp-named roots and refuse corrupt roots; atomic temporary ref publication uses only the reserved lock namespace with independent failing reverts.
expected_result: GC and listing retain every legal tmp-named ref and directory; corrupt tmp refs refuse deletion; atomic ref temporary files occupy only the reserved lock namespace and never overwrite a valid ref; independent behavioural revert regressions fail.
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/138, merged 2026-10-22T22:03:12Z, merge 69164ec133ecca8f5bcb9a72d465f1830135151f: GC/listing retain legal tmp-named roots and refuse corrupt roots; atomic temporary ref publication uses only the reserved lock namespace with independent failing reverts."
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T17:19:37.543Z",codex-agent,"Verified 36/36 ref and GC tests, both directly and through pm test --run --progress. Function-only behavioral reverts independently fail: restoring writeAtomic loses the process-shaped tmp ref; restoring RefStore.list hides a legal tmp ref; restoring refRoots fails both retained-root cases and corrupt-root refusal. Native CLI acceptance also passed with only Node on PATH and a fatal Git interceptor, including tmp-branch listing and applied GC retention. No existing ref or oplog data was trimmed."
  "2026-10-21T21:15:54.583Z",codex-agent,"PR 138 unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6u84nm is valid: fail-closed malformed-ref refusal omits the offending path. Include the ref path while retaining pre-sweep refusal; extend regression to assert the exact error and retained garbage. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-21T21:18:36.528Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: replacing only refRoots with the fetched PR-head function makes all four targeted GC regressions fail (0/4 pass): empty and partial tmp refs omit the offending path, as do ref-file and ref-directory symlinks. Restoring the fix passes all four, retaining fail-closed collection and every synthetic unreachable object on refusal. Exact command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^GC refuses a corrupt tmp-named ref|^bad upload roots|^dangling links\" test/gc.test.ts."
  "2026-10-22T10:59:25.444Z",codex-agent,"Continuation round for PR 138: pulled the remote head and confirmed current main is already included; no interrupted draft edits or unpushed commits were present. Read every unresolved thread comment and the latest CodeRabbit review, which has no outside-diff section. Thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6vAP0c is valid: writeAtomic removes no reserved random temp after write, fsync, close or rename failure. Whole-diff review found the same write/fsync/close cleanup gap in ObjectStore.writeRaw, whose existing catch covers rename only. Extend cleanup over the whole owned publication in both locations; add eight real plain-directory regressions with descriptor-scoped filesystem fault injection, checking exact error identity, closed descriptors, preserved prior data and unrelated files, and successful retry. No pm SDK mocks or Git dependency."
  "2026-10-22T11:01:32.581Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs completed before archive generation. Reverting only writeAtomic to the fetched head makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^atomic ref publication\" test/atomic-publication-cleanup.test.ts fail 0/5; restoring it passes 5/5. Reverting only ObjectStore.writeRaw makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^atomic object publication\" test/atomic-publication-cleanup.test.ts pass 1/4 and fail 3/4: write/fsync/close leave owned temp files, while the existing rename cleanup still passes. Restoring it passes 4/4. Full new file passes 9/9, including a repeated native rename refusal without fault injection, with all functions restored. Tests import source directly, so no dist rebuild is required for proof. Bun real-ref suite passes 12/12. Pinned npm ci, source/test typechecks, lint and zero-duplication checks pass; thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T11:03:01.873Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation receipt for PR 138: linked pm test run passes 3/3 commands with 37 ref/GC tests, 4 focused fail-closed GC tests and 9 cleanup tests (50 executions, zero failures/skips/cancellations). ObjectStore tests separately pass 14/14. Bun runs pass 12/12 real-ref tests and 1/1 selected native cleanup regression. Build, source/test typechecks, lint, docstrings and the 0% duplication gate pass. Strict pm health passes with the CI-pinned project extension; only two pre-existing advisory warnings remain, and history is append-only. dist is ignored, not committed. The restored production functions and tracker are staged before deterministic archive generation. Full unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release gates on Node 22/26 are required at the final-head receipt https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/138/checks; those exact-head CI results are authoritative for full-suite counts. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress. No review replies/resolutions, merge, release, dependency bump or out-of-scope service changes."
  "2026-10-22T14:43:07.673Z",codex-agent,"New review round: remote head pulled clean, main already included. Reviewing PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6vOcn7: the nested lock fixture needs an assertion over every path segment. Retaining the completed atomic cleanup implementation and its independent proofs. This round will strengthen the test and prove it detects removal of the directory lock filter."
  "2026-10-22T14:45:55.853Z",codex-agent,"The refs.list test now rejects a reserved .lock suffix in every returned path segment, covering abandoned.lock/not-a-ref. Independent control: changing only RefStore.list's lock filter to skip lock files while traversing lock directories lets the original test pass 1/1, but the strengthened assertion fails 0/1. Restoring the production filter passes 1/1. Exact command: node --test --test-name-pattern='^list walks valid tmp refs' test/refs.test.ts. The two selected restored regressions pass 2/2 with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Production files are byte-identical to the pulled head after the proof; no runtime change is needed. Whole-PR review found no other instance of this assertion gap."
  "2026-10-22T14:48:48.387Z",codex-agent,"Round-two linked validation passes via pinned pm test pm-vcs-phase6tmprefs --run --only-index 1 --progress: 37/37 ref/GC tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations. The staging linked command passes 9/9, and the two selected native Bun regressions pass 2/2 with 19 unrelated cases filtered. Build, test compilation and static gates pass. Prior owned-temp cleanup code and its independent proofs are retained. Complete final-head npm release-check steps and bun run release:check remain required at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/138/checks. Both review findings are valid, fixed in tests and backed by original-passes/strengthened-fails production-guard controls. Releasing the claim for CI and orchestrator verification; the item stays in_progress."
